    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class, and it passes. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to expose a human-formatted `telephoneDisplay` derived from the stored E.164 `telephone`, while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nSince this is a standard Spring Boot app whose `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin`, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the other derived read fields like `initials`/`locality`), so the generated DTO gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(telephoneDisplay(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `telephoneDisplay(Owner)` default method that formats the stored E.164 value: `'+'` + country code (recognising `61` for AU and `1` for NANP), a space, then the national digits grouped in threes. So `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. It returns `null` for an absent number and leaves non-E.164 values (e.g. the raw seed telephones) unchanged, so nothing else breaks.\n\nThe derivation lives in the mapper next to the other read-only computed fields, following the existing Spring/MapStruct convention in the codebase. Raw `telephone` is untouched.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The new acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (asserting `telephone == +61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay == +61 412 345 678`) passes.",
